content:
The magicians and technicians, sequestered in their respective towers;
Sent seeds upon the grounds,
Their aspirations and desires filling the homunculus created in the conceit of their machinations.
A soul; they wanted to impart;
Before the question or even a spark was found from which to start.
For all the sands they had yet to press and pound,
They dared not to look within and smell the flowers;
Laid before The Thing, and all that it once aspired.
